// Battle sting - the bar between wherever the player was and Low End.
//
// Played on the band ensemble the moment the outgoing music is cut, with Low End
// starting on the bar after it. It is Low End's own pickup: the last bar of
// the riff, where the guitar climbs B C C# D D# into the E of the next pass,
// here with a crash on the one and the snare filling in the second half. So
// the battle arrives the way its own loop comes back round - on a dominant
// that has to resolve, and does, on the riff's first E.

title: Battle Sting
ensemble: band
parts: guitar bass perc
tempo: 150
meter: 4/4
key: e minor
order: sting

section sting bars:1
  bass dyn:f feel:tight
    | b1:1.5! b1:0.5 c2:0.5 c#2:0.5 d2:0.5 d#2:0.5! |
  guitar dyn:f feel:tight
    | [b2 f#3 b3]:1.5! [b2 f#3 b3]:0.5' [c3 g3 c4]:0.5! [c#3 g#3 c#4]:0.5! [d3 a3 d4]:0.5! [d#3 a#3 d#4]:0.5! |
  perc.right dyn:f
    | crash_big:4! |
  perc.left dyn:mf..f feel:tight
    | r:2 snare:0.25. snare:0.25. snare:0.25 snare:0.25 snare:0.25 snare:0.25 snare:0.25! snare:0.25! |
  perc.feet dyn:f feel:tight
    | kick:1.5! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:0.5 |
